Generated by scripts/record_semicolon_data.py from the real RuboCop 1.89.0 CLI under Ruby 4.0.8.
Recorded 2026-10-23: 18 sources x 2 target/engine profiles (2.7/parser_whitequark and
3.4/parser_prism) x LF/CRLF x inspect/-a/-A = 216 file conditions, followed by the same
invocation on its actual corrected disk output. Every report field, summary, exit and
corrected byte is preserved. Raw reference after bytes are stored separately from the
expected Sonicop CRLF-preserving format.

Sources marked with data_before_hex execute STDOUT.write(DATA.read) under MRI 2.7.8.
The original, raw upstream output and CRLF-preserving expected output are all run as
scripts. The expected output must return exactly the original DATA.read bytes, including
empty data, missing final newlines, UTF-8, SOH, and semicolons. Controls distinguish code
before DATA, literals/heredocs/comments containing similar text, and ordinary code.
